<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.bekh.eva-stream-analyst</string>
    <!-- The fourth voice: the analyst. One run reads the last eight dreams fresh and writes
         the portrait, then exits; the ribbon's line is the portrait's closing, cut by the tool.

         **No interval, on purpose** (2026-09-23): the clock is the tap. stream.py kickstarts
         this job with the other voices after a page lands (STREAM_KICK_INTERPRETER=1 in
         com.bekh.eva-stream.plist), and the run is a quiet no-op until four new unflagged
         dreams sit above his watermark — so three taps in four cost a directory walk and
         no call, and the fourth puts the portrait right after the dream that completed it.

         Putting a StartInterval back breaks nothing; it only wakes him to count and exit. A
         lost kick costs nothing at all: the dreams stay above the watermark and the next tap
         takes them. A backlog (the stream ran while he was off) is chewed one batch per landing.

         Loading this job runs nothing (RunAtLoad false). By hand:
             launchctl kickstart gui/$(id -u)/com.bekh.eva-stream-analyst
             uv run --python 3.12 eva/stream/analyst.py --once

         The seat is STREAM_ANALYST_SEAT, unset here and so `analyst` — the one seat the loom
         puts on the api. Needs `claude` logged in on this machine; not llama, not the loom. -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/uv</string>
        <string>run</string>
        <string>--python</string>
        <string>3.12</string>
        <string>/Users/bekh/tower/forge/eva-goes-berserk/eva/stream/analyst.py</string>
        <string>--once</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>/Users/bekh/tower/forge/eva-goes-berserk</string>
    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <!-- ~/.local/bin is where `claude` lives and launchd's default PATH has not heard of
             it; without this every run is a ledger row saying "no `claude` on PATH".
             /opt/homebrew/bin is uv. -->
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>/Users/bekh/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
        <!-- claude reads the login keychain and ~/.claude through HOME; a launchd job without
             one authenticates as nobody and exits non-zero. -->
        <key>HOME</key>
        <string>/Users/bekh</string>
        <!-- bekh, 2026-09-23, late: GPT (sol through codex), a fresh read of the last eight
             dreams every four — a portrait per story, each reading two (bekh, 2026-09-24) — no session, nothing resumed.
             The student (deepseek, thirty every eight) ran for one evening and was retired:
             its lines read as captions of the last dream. -->
        <key>STREAM_ANALYST_DOOR</key>
        <string>codex</string>
        <key>STREAM_ANALYST_WINDOW</key>
        <string>8</string>
        <key>STREAM_ANALYST_EVERY</key>
        <string>4</string>
    </dict>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/eva-stream-analyst.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/eva-stream-analyst.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
